## Context and authority

Child of 1572; author ruling relayed by the author’s own interface session
/root and recorded on the parent at 2026-11-27T11:42Z. Recording is a truthful relay,
not an agent-written author signature. The author authorized raid delivery
through review, gates, eligible merge, and roar. No implementation has begun.

## Scope

Implement two generic, reusable probe-plan approval modes. First, the author
may approve the identified plan in its file or in conversation; preserve the
actual author signature separately from a truthful, provenance-bearing
transcription. Second, the author may explicitly delegate plan approval to a
panel for a defined campaign and fixed perimeter; retain the author’s delegation,
plan/version, panel opinions/disagreements, conditions, and approval record.
A driver supplies scope and provenance but cannot self-grant authority. Amendments
need approval within the authorized perimeter; outside it, return to the author.
Reconcile agents-never-write-signature statements without impersonating an author
or granting permanent panel authority. Keep driver, project, cohort, and model
names out of generic policy. Auto-blog, scientific monitoring, and climate-finance
meta-analysis are examples of genericity only, not authorized pipelines. Preserve
outward publication/contact and paid-spend boundaries and existing scope/scoring.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author approval in file or conversation is supported with identified plan/version and truthful approval-transcription provenance distinct from an actual author-written signature.
- [ ] Explicit bounded campaign delegation supports panel approval only within the fixed author-defined perimeter, retaining opinions/disagreements, conditions, and amendment approvals; no driver self-authorization or permanent panel power.
- [ ] All signature/approval parallel units are reconciled without impersonation or hard-coded driver/project/model names; no new pipeline, publication, contact, spending, or unrelated scoring authority is introduced.

## Plan and first verification

Documentation and contracts, not new estimates or an orchestration service.
Read current SKILL.md and parallel references as one logical unit, then map
each change to the author ruling. First verification is a source/scenario
audit with a positive control, a boundary case, and a counterexample that
would expose scope or authority drift. Preserve unresolved evidence. Do not
add tests pinning prose wording. Run required adherence and project hygiene
checks, distinct semantic review, gaze, and the caller’s gate/merge route.

## Feasibility and dependencies

PASS: current skill/reference paths exist, with no scientific data, licence,
API key, or paid route needed. Shared contracts require sequential delivery.
No three-PR concurrent registry edit or coordination PR is needed. No foreign
project edits or rereads are required.
